From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:30:00 +0000
Subject: arm64: dts: rockchip: rock-pi-4: disable S/PDIF card by default

The sound-dit card links to the S/PDIF controller, which is disabled.
The card cannot probe and logs a deferred probe parse error on every
boot. Disable the card. The rk3399-rock-pi-4-spdif overlay enables
both the controller and the card.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-pi-4.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-pi-4.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-pi-4.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-pi-4.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-pi-4.dtsi
@@ -59,6 +59,7 @@ sound-dit {
 		compatible = "audio-graph-card";
 		label = "SPDIF";
 		dais = <&spdif_p0>;
+		status = "disabled";
 	};
 
 	spdif-dit {
-- 
Armbian

